WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:04.620
Scrolling through all the options on Netflix
may end up taking up your whole night — so

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.400
we're here to help you narrow it down.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.620
If you're looking to park it on the couch
and dive into a heart-pounding thriller, here

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.360
are some hidden gems worth checking out.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.100
Cheap Thrills

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.580
A bloody, pervy thrill-ride, Cheap Thrills
follows a writer-slash-auto mechanic named

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.800
Craig, who's fired from his job on the same
day he gets an eviction notice.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.600
Depressed, Craig winds up in a bar where he
catches the attention of a sociopathic couple

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.020
with too much time and money on their hands.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.720
"Whichever of you fellas that does this shot
first gets 50 bucks Boom!"

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.710
The couple offers cash to Craig and his friend
if they carry out a series of escalating dares,

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.100
each a little worse than the one before.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:47.579
The tension ratchets up with each challenge,
until its horrific final shot, an image that'll

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.680
leave you wondering what you would do for
the right amount of money.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.820
The Two Faces of January

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:59.039
Set in 1960s Greece, The Two Faces of January
follows a wealthy American couple, played

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.620
by Viggo Mortensen and Kirsten Dunst.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.720
They run across a shady yet charming grifter,
played by Oscar Isaac, who makes his living

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.070
swindling tourists.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:11.780
Soon enough, the trio is covering up a crime
and running from the cops.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.080
If you're in the mood for something simmering
and suspenseful — complete with an exotic

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:21.030
locale and plenty of pretty faces hiding all
sorts of dirty secrets — then check out

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.180
this Hitchcockian film.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.520
The Stanford Prison Experiment

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.300
Inspired by the most infamous study in the
history of psychology, The Stanford Prison

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.860
Experiment will leave you battered, bruised,
and gasping for breath.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.280
The film follows a group of college students
selected to take part in the scariest role-playing

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.760
exercise of all time.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.160
Half are assigned the part of prisoners, and
the others are given guard duty.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:49.020
"From this point forward, you should never
refer to this as study or experiment again."

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:53.530
It's a grueling experience, made all the more
intense by its talented young stars.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:57.480
If it weren't based on a true story, this
would feel like a horror movie.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:02.440
Instead, it's a gritty reflection of the abuse
of power in our world — which is far more

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.180
terrifying.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.780
The Trust

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:10.479
In the underrated thriller The Trust, Nicolas
Cage and Elijah Wood play cops who are sick

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:15.760
of their lives and hoping to turn things around
by cracking a massive safe owned by criminals,

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.500
hidden inside a grocery store.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.560
The duo quickly assembles a plan to pull off
the heist, but while the first half of the

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:27.150
film goes by fast, the second half slows down
as they put their plan into action... and

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.840
it's here that The Trust truly shines.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.790
Throw in a killer ending, and you've got a
bizarre little thriller that totally deserves

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:34.420
your attention.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.080
I Don't Feel At Home in This World Anymore

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.760
Critically speaking, I Don't Feel at Home
in This World Anymore was a smash hit, winning

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.640
the Grand Jury Award at the Sundance Film
Festival.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:50.090
Still, this wildly entertaining film hasn't
gotten enough mainstream love, and it definitely

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:51.540
deserves a bigger fanbase.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:57.220
The story follows an increasingly frustrated
nurse named Ruth, played by Melanie Lynskey.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.880
"You've been s------ in my yard."

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.080
"I have not."

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:02.480
"Your dog."

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.960
Every day, Ruth notices that people are just
awful.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.760
Unwilling to take it anymore, Ruth joins up
with her antisocial neighbor, played by Elijah

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.820
Wood, to bring the crooks to justice.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:18.080
Wood is hilarious as a wannabe tough guy,
and Lynskey might be the most relatable protagonist

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.200
in cinematic history.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.819
All this frustrated nurse wants is for people
to stop being jerks, and if you don't shape

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.620
up, she's going to track you down and teach
you some manners.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:28.080
Wheelman

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:35.040
Shot almost exclusively inside a nondescript
BMW, Wheelman is a claustrophobic thriller,

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.430
a movie that makes you feel just as trapped
and helpless as its hero, played by Frank

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:39.930
Grillo.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.800
The film follows a nameless getaway driver
who's sucked into a game of cat-and-mouse.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:49.050
He begins juggling phone calls as he works
his way up and down city streets, trying to

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:53.580
discover who's pulling the strings, all while
keeping his teenage daughter out of harm's

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.080
way.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:59.120
The tension slowly ratchets up for Grillo,
who attempts to puzzle his way out of a job

00:03:59.120 --> 00:03:59.620
gone wrong.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.680
Grillo is at the top of his game here, and
if this were a just and fair world, his performance

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.720
in Wheelman would turn this guy into an A-list
star.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:09.480
Mother

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:16.060
Equal parts social satire, slapstick comedy,
and dark mystery, Mother follows an unnamed

00:04:16.079 --> 00:04:21.410
herbalist who's determined to prove her mentally
handicapped son is innocent after he's arrested

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.280
for a brutal crime.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:25.640
That's easier said than done, as nobody believes
her story.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.900
But as she digs deeper into the case, she's
eventually forced to make a decision that

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.740
proves there's nothing more powerful than
a mother's love.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:38.170
Snowpiercer director Bong Joon-ho is such
a skilled filmmaker that you'll be sitting

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.180
on the edge of your seat.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:43.260
And no matter how many suspense flicks you've
seen before, you won't be able to guess where

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:43.920
this film is headed.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.260
Thanks for watching!

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.820
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.380
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

